invariant: INV-28
file: handshake_post.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: inv55-key-update-answer-per-request's edit, with the tcp-nonblocking
  loop as the catcher: ch_read calls cfg.send to answer a KeyUpdate, which
  a caller whose send holds only input during ch_read, as colibri's does,
  does not expect. The connected server reads a request, and the loop
  requires that read to call cfg.send no time.

--- old
    if (request == 1 && t->send_epochs < HSPOST_SEND_EPOCHS_MAX) {
        t->key_update_owed = 1;
    }
--- new
    if (request == 1 && t->send_epochs < HSPOST_SEND_EPOCHS_MAX) {
        (void)hspost_send_key_update(t);
    }
